Okay. But you should
know, in open court,

258
00:20:26,125 --> 00:20:28,685
they'll hold you in
contempt if you don't answer.

259
00:20:30,463 --> 00:20:32,022
Who said anything about court?

260
00:20:32,465 --> 00:20:34,934
Me. See you.

261
00:20:35,501 --> 00:20:37,026
Wait a minute. Where you going?

262
00:20:37,203 --> 00:20:39,104
- I'm buzzing off.
- Wait.

263
00:20:39,939 --> 00:20:41,168
Wait.

264
00:20:44,076 --> 00:20:47,240
This is really embarrassing.

265
00:20:47,413 --> 00:20:51,316
My boyfriend was having an
affair with Helaine Cameron.

266
00:20:51,484 --> 00:20:53,646
I followed him there.

267
00:20:54,086 --> 00:20:55,145
I was so angry

268
00:20:55,321 --> 00:20:58,189
that I wanted to go in
there and do something.

269
00:20:58,357 --> 00:20:59,916
I don't know what.

270
00:21:00,092 --> 00:21:05,030
Then I came to my
senses, and I went home.

271
00:21:07,266 --> 00:21:09,963
- For the night?
- Huh?

272
00:21:10,803 --> 00:21:11,803
By yourself?

273
00:21:11,971 --> 00:21:14,133
Your boyfriend didn't come?

274
00:21:14,306 --> 00:21:15,831
Uh-uh.

275
00:21:16,342 --> 00:21:19,141
- His name Wayne?
- Yeah.

276
00:21:19,512 --> 00:21:21,481
How did you know that?

277
00:21:22,181 --> 00:21:24,150
Everybody knows that.

278
00:21:31,123 --> 00:21:33,285
- I don't wanna play gin, dad.
- Seven...

279
00:21:33,459 --> 00:21:38,830
seven, eight, eight,
nine, nine, ten, ten.

280
00:21:38,998 --> 00:21:40,990
Dad, it just upsets you.

281
00:21:41,167 --> 00:21:43,193
Did I throw my
cards the other night?

282
00:21:43,369 --> 00:21:45,449
No. But you didn't talk to
me for an hour and a half.

283
00:21:45,604 --> 00:21:47,698
I didn't feel good. I
had a stomachache.

284
00:21:47,873 --> 00:21:50,206
I feel better now. Come on.

285
00:21:53,779 --> 00:21:56,715
Your little winning streak
of seven straight hands

286
00:21:56,882 --> 00:21:58,441
is about to come to an end.

287
00:21:58,617 --> 00:22:01,587
- Nine. Nine straight hands.
- Oh.

288
00:22:01,754 --> 00:22:02,949
Pick a card.

289
00:22:10,329 --> 00:22:11,991
Ho, ho. Ho-ho-ho.

290
00:22:12,164 --> 00:22:15,965
That's gonna fill a
nice little hole right here.

291
00:22:19,672 --> 00:22:21,265
Okay. Now, isn't this fun?

292
00:22:21,640 --> 00:22:24,109
- It's a joy, Dad.
- Mm-hm.

293
00:22:25,811 --> 00:22:27,609
Ah.

294
00:22:31,050 --> 00:22:37,081
Something tells me
you need this little card.

295
00:22:37,690 --> 00:22:39,522
No.

296
00:22:39,692 --> 00:22:42,161
You don't need this little card.

297
00:22:47,433 --> 00:22:48,901
Gin.

298
00:22:58,077 --> 00:22:59,511
You looking mighty pretty.

299
00:22:59,678 --> 00:23:01,772
Why don't you get
out of here? I mean...

300
00:23:01,947 --> 00:23:03,438
- Unh.
- Isn't that what you want?

301
00:23:03,616 --> 00:23:06,085
I frighten you,
and you like that.

302
00:23:06,252 --> 00:23:09,222
- You revolt me.
- You were staring at me.

303
00:23:09,388 --> 00:23:12,984
You think about me when you get into
bed with that sweet husband of yours?

304
00:23:17,763 --> 00:23:20,665
I liked that. You
like to play rough.

305
00:23:23,903 --> 00:23:26,737
Wayne, try to keep it sexy.

306
00:23:29,174 --> 00:23:30,665
Dad.

307
00:23:32,111 --> 00:23:34,842
- They were rehearsing that scene.
- Yeah.

308
00:23:39,919 --> 00:23:41,080
Excuse me.

309
00:23:41,487 --> 00:23:42,887
I'm sorry.

310
00:23:43,455 --> 00:23:45,151
Excuse me, Mr. Drummond.

311
00:23:46,025 --> 00:23:48,221
Hello. My name
is Leanne Mclntyre.

312
00:23:48,394 --> 00:23:51,091
I'm representing Philip
Cameron in the murder trial.

313
00:23:51,263 --> 00:23:54,756
I was wondering if I could
ask you a couple of questions.

314
00:23:56,035 --> 00:23:57,059
Take five.

315
00:23:57,670 --> 00:23:59,502
Thank you.

316
00:24:02,841 --> 00:24:05,122
Mr. Drummond, I'd like you to
meet my father, Ben Matlock.

317
00:24:05,277 --> 00:24:07,007
- Hi.
- I saw you

318
00:24:07,179 --> 00:24:10,616
at Helaine Cameron's
house the night she died.

319
00:24:10,783 --> 00:24:13,343
Were you working on this scene?

320
00:24:13,519 --> 00:24:16,421
Yeah. That's her understudy.

321
00:24:16,855 --> 00:24:21,691
I guess that's what made it
look like you were fighting.

322
00:24:21,860 --> 00:24:24,420
This scene.

323
00:24:24,596 --> 00:24:25,996
How much did you see?

324
00:24:26,165 --> 00:24:28,930
Did Helaine break
up with you that night?

325
00:24:34,139 --> 00:24:35,437
- No.
- Did she tell you

326
00:24:35,607 --> 00:24:37,701
she was never
gonna see you again?

327
00:24:37,876 --> 00:24:39,868
We were making plans to
spend the weekend together

328
00:24:40,045 --> 00:24:42,446
when her husband
went out of town.

329
00:24:42,748 --> 00:24:44,944
Who told you she
was going to end it?

330
00:24:45,117 --> 00:24:47,677
Her husband? Is
that what he said?

331
00:24:47,853 --> 00:24:49,412
He said that he and Helaine

332
00:24:49,588 --> 00:24:52,217
were gonna put their
marriage back together.

333
00:24:52,391 --> 00:24:53,757
That's a lie.

334
00:24:53,926 --> 00:24:56,657
I loved Helaine
and she loved me.

335
00:24:56,829 --> 00:24:59,264
She was alive when I left.

336
00:25:00,099 --> 00:25:01,328
Very much alive.

337
00:25:02,668 --> 00:25:04,364
Well, we've taken up
enough of your time.

338
00:25:04,536 --> 00:25:06,368
Thanks very much.

339
00:25:09,942 --> 00:25:13,401
You know, there's
another way to look at this.

340
00:25:13,579 --> 00:25:16,310
Maybe Helaine asked
him for a divorce.

341
00:25:16,482 --> 00:25:18,781
Maybe that's why he killed her.

342
00:25:26,258 --> 00:25:30,161
Maybe I misunderstood
everything I saw.

343
00:25:58,023 --> 00:25:59,023
So, what do you think?

344
00:26:12,438 --> 00:26:15,272
<i>He grabbed her and tried
to kiss her, she slapped him,</i>

345
00:26:15,441 --> 00:26:17,535
<i>then he went for her
and grabbed her again.</i>

346
00:26:20,679 --> 00:26:23,513
That's just what
happened in the play.

347
00:26:23,682 --> 00:26:26,083
So where does that leave us?

348
00:26:37,229 --> 00:26:42,861
Someone was in the house
when Philip Cameron came home.

349
00:26:43,135 --> 00:26:45,866
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

350
00:26:46,105 --> 00:26:48,074
That's all we need.

351
00:26:53,846 --> 00:26:55,542
Miss Galloway,

352
00:26:55,714 --> 00:26:59,310
how long have you lived next
door to Philip and Helaine Cameron?

353
00:26:59,485 --> 00:27:01,454
Four years, ever
since they moved in.

354
00:27:01,620 --> 00:27:03,380
Did they seem like they
were happily married?

355
00:27:03,522 --> 00:27:04,751
Objection, Your Honor.

356
00:27:04,923 --> 00:27:06,858
No foundation. Calls
for a speculation.

357
00:27:07,025 --> 00:27:08,025
I'll rephrase.

358
00:27:08,193 --> 00:27:10,389
Miss Galloway, in
the last six months,

359
00:27:10,562 --> 00:27:13,191
did you witness any fights between
Philip and Helaine Cameron?

360
00:27:13,365 --> 00:27:15,163
Oh, yes, I have.

361
00:27:15,701 --> 00:27:17,621
And were you aware what
they were fighting about?

362
00:27:17,769 --> 00:27:19,067
It was very clear.

363
00:27:19,238 --> 00:27:21,104
Mr. Cameron was very angry.

364
00:27:21,273 --> 00:27:25,005
He told his wife that she would
have to stop seeing another man.

365
00:27:25,177 --> 00:27:27,612
He told her that she was
destroying their marriage,

366
00:27:27,779 --> 00:27:29,111
and he wouldn't stand for it.

367
00:27:29,281 --> 00:27:32,251
You say he was very
upset and very angry?

368
00:27:32,518 --> 00:27:33,518
Very.

369
00:27:34,286 --> 00:27:36,118
Thank you.

370
00:27:39,291 --> 00:27:42,489
So Chinese, Italian, what
do you feel like tonight?

371
00:27:44,096 --> 00:27:47,157
Wayne, listen,

372
00:27:48,634 --> 00:27:52,298
a lawyer named Ben Matlock
came in to see me yesterday.

373
00:27:52,771 --> 00:27:53,864
What's he want with you?

374
00:27:54,940 --> 00:27:58,069
He saw me outside
the Camerons' house

375
00:27:58,343 --> 00:28:00,073
the night that Helaine
Cameron was murdered.

376
00:28:00,245 --> 00:28:03,147
You were outside the house?
What were you doing there?

377
00:28:03,482 --> 00:28:05,644
I followed you there.

378
00:28:16,528 --> 00:28:18,224
I knew about you and Helaine.

379
00:28:20,065 --> 00:28:21,897
I'm sorry.

380
00:28:22,901 --> 00:28:24,733
I didn't mean to hurt you.

381
00:28:25,604 --> 00:28:29,700
Wayne, you know I love you,
and I don't wanna lose you.

382
00:28:29,875 --> 00:28:31,639
But if you're gonna
carry on like this,

383
00:28:31,810 --> 00:28:35,178
then I think that we should
just end it here, right now,

384
00:28:35,347 --> 00:28:36,781
before things get any worse.

385
00:28:44,056 --> 00:28:47,288
I'd really like to try and
make this up to you.

386
00:28:53,999 --> 00:28:55,695
Hey.

387
00:28:55,867 --> 00:28:57,335
When we got to
the Cameron house,

388
00:28:57,502 --> 00:28:59,471
Philip Cameron said he
just got home from work,

389
00:28:59,638 --> 00:29:01,072
found his wife dead.

390
00:29:01,240 --> 00:29:03,971
We did a thorough
examination of the crime scene.

391
00:29:04,142 --> 00:29:05,633
Hmm.

392
00:29:11,250 --> 00:29:13,742
Did you find the murder
weapon, detective?

393
00:29:13,919 --> 00:29:16,388
Yes, sir. It was a
6-inch carving knife.

394
00:29:16,555 --> 00:29:18,581
Did you find any
fingerprints on the knife?

395
00:29:18,757 --> 00:29:19,850
Yes, sir, we did.

396
00:29:20,025 --> 00:29:23,427
By the morning, we were able
to establish two sets of prints.

397
00:29:23,829 --> 00:29:27,766
The victim's, Helaine Cameron,
and the defendant, Philip Cameron.

398
00:29:28,467 --> 00:29:31,801
It was at that time that we
placed Mr. Cameron under arrest.

399
00:29:31,970 --> 00:29:34,565
Thank you. Nothing further.

400
00:29:35,440 --> 00:29:36,703
Miss Mclntyre.

401
00:29:38,477 --> 00:29:39,775
Miss Mclntyre.

402
00:29:39,945 --> 00:29:41,709
Yes, Your Honor.

403
00:29:42,514 --> 00:29:45,006
Detective Cavallo, did
you tell Mr. Cameron

404
00:29:45,183 --> 00:29:46,776
that his fingerprints
were on the knife?

405
00:29:46,952 --> 00:29:48,921
- Yes, I did.
- What did he say?

406
00:29:49,087 --> 00:29:51,318
He said that it was the
only sharp knife in the house,

407
00:29:51,490 --> 00:29:54,289
and that he used it to carve
three or four times a week.

408
00:29:54,459 --> 00:29:55,893
Thank you.

409
00:29:56,061 --> 00:29:57,256
Mr. Wygot.

410
00:29:58,297 --> 00:30:00,027
The state rests, Your Honor.

411
00:30:00,832 --> 00:30:01,959
Is the defense ready?

412
00:30:02,134 --> 00:30:04,228
Yes, we are, Your Honor,
and for my first witness,

413
00:30:04,403 --> 00:30:07,339
I would like to call
Mr. Benjamin Matlock.

414
00:30:13,211 --> 00:30:15,407
Conrad? CONRAD: <i>Yo.</i>

415
00:30:15,580 --> 00:30:17,139
- You following Karen?
<i>- Yeah.</i>

416
00:30:17,316 --> 00:30:20,980
Right now she's outside the
Cameron house, sitting in her car.

417
00:30:21,420 --> 00:30:22,820
What's she doing in her car?

418
00:30:22,988 --> 00:30:24,650
I give up.

419
00:30:24,890 --> 00:30:26,085
I just followed her here.

420
00:30:26,258 --> 00:30:29,092
First, she was with
Wayne at the bar.

421
00:30:29,261 --> 00:30:30,320
Then she came here.

422
00:30:30,495 --> 00:30:33,021
And right now, all she's
doing is sitting in her car,

423
00:30:33,231 --> 00:30:34,358
watching the house.

424
00:30:34,533 --> 00:30:37,401
- Anybody in there?
<i>- Uh, nope.</i>

425
00:30:38,970 --> 00:30:40,097
Dad. Come on.

426
00:30:40,272 --> 00:30:41,433
Come on.

427
00:30:41,606 --> 00:30:44,838
Conrad, stay on her. I gotta go.

428
00:30:45,377 --> 00:30:46,845
Okay.

429
00:30:48,013 --> 00:30:51,950
Mr. Matlock, where were you on
the night of Saturday, March 18th?

430
00:30:52,117 --> 00:30:54,416
- The Wilmont Hotel.
- Situated where?

431
00:30:54,586 --> 00:30:56,987
3231 Oleander Drive.

432
00:30:57,155 --> 00:31:00,284
That's right across the street
from 3230 Oleander Drive,

433
00:31:00,459 --> 00:31:02,223
- the Camerons' house.
- That's right.

434
00:31:02,828 --> 00:31:05,992
That night, did you have a clear
view of the Camerons' house

435
00:31:06,164 --> 00:31:07,393
from your hotel window?

436
00:31:07,566 --> 00:31:10,092
Yes. I could see
directly into the den.

437
00:31:10,268 --> 00:31:13,204
At around midnight, did you
see Mr. Cameron coming home?

438
00:31:13,372 --> 00:31:16,672
Yes. I saw Mr. Cameron
drive his car up to his garage.

439
00:31:16,842 --> 00:31:18,743
At that time, did you
see anything else?

440
00:31:18,910 --> 00:31:20,742
Yeah. The minute he
slammed his car door,

441
00:31:20,912 --> 00:31:23,575
I saw a shadowy
figure run from the den

442
00:31:23,749 --> 00:31:25,081
and out the side of the garage.

443
00:31:25,350 --> 00:31:27,410
Let me make sure
I understand you.

444
00:31:27,586 --> 00:31:29,521
You're saying that someone
else was in the house

445
00:31:29,688 --> 00:31:30,928
when Mr. Cameron returned home.

446
00:31:31,056 --> 00:31:32,183
I'm certain of it.

447
00:31:32,524 --> 00:31:34,356
Thank you, Mr. Matlock.

448
00:32:26,545 --> 00:32:29,014
What brought you to the
Wilmont Hotel, Mr. Matlock?

449
00:32:29,181 --> 00:32:31,116
Fellow I know is
getting married.

450
00:32:31,283 --> 00:32:32,808
How was the wedding?

451
00:32:32,984 --> 00:32:36,284
- I, uh, I didn't go.
- Why not?

452
00:32:36,922 --> 00:32:38,390
I wasn't feeling well.

453
00:32:38,557 --> 00:32:40,492
Well, you must have
been feeling pretty sick

454
00:32:40,659 --> 00:32:42,560
to drive all the way
from Willow Springs

455
00:32:42,727 --> 00:32:46,095
- then decide not to go to the wedding.
- It was just a little stomachache.

456
00:32:46,465 --> 00:32:49,958
Did you take any medication
for this little stomachache?

457
00:32:50,135 --> 00:32:51,831
The doctor prescribed something.

458
00:32:52,003 --> 00:32:54,996
Something that
required a prescription.

459
00:32:55,607 --> 00:33:00,272
Was there any narcotic in it,
something to help you sleep?

460
00:33:00,912 --> 00:33:02,540
Um...

461
00:33:03,782 --> 00:33:04,875
Maybe.

462
00:33:05,050 --> 00:33:09,545
How far away do you think your
window at the Wilmont Hotel was

463
00:33:09,721 --> 00:33:10,916
from the Camerons' house?

464
00:33:11,089 --> 00:33:12,421
I don't know.

465
00:33:12,824 --> 00:33:14,588
Please, your best guess.

466
00:33:15,026 --> 00:33:16,654
Um...

467
00:33:17,229 --> 00:33:20,063
Forty, 50 yards.

468
00:33:20,232 --> 00:33:22,428
And while you were
peeping from this window,

469
00:33:22,601 --> 00:33:23,864
you saw this shadowy figure.

470
00:33:24,035 --> 00:33:26,937
- I wasn't peeping.
- Objection, Your Honor.

471
00:33:27,105 --> 00:33:28,437
Sustained. Mr. Wygot.

472
00:33:28,607 --> 00:33:30,838
The very idea! Peeping.

473
00:33:31,009 --> 00:33:32,009
Mr. Matlock.

474
00:33:32,177 --> 00:33:34,646
- Your Honor, you know me.
- Dad.

475
00:33:34,813 --> 00:33:36,441
He said I was peeping.

476
00:33:36,615 --> 00:33:37,981
How dare you!

477
00:33:38,650 --> 00:33:39,811
May I continue?

478
00:33:40,685 --> 00:33:42,654
- Go ahead.
- Peeping.

479
00:33:42,921 --> 00:33:46,688
Mr. Matlock, are you sure
you saw the shadowy figure?

480
00:33:46,858 --> 00:33:48,622
Yes.

481
00:33:48,894 --> 00:33:51,887
Was he tall, short,

482
00:33:52,264 --> 00:33:57,999
fat, thin, black,
white, man or woman?

483
00:33:58,169 --> 00:34:01,606
You're not really sure
who or even what you saw.

484
00:34:01,773 --> 00:34:04,641
- Are you, Mr. Matlock?
- I saw somebody.

485
00:34:04,809 --> 00:34:06,243
Let's be perfectly clear

486
00:34:06,411 --> 00:34:08,642
about what happened on
Saturday night, March the 18th.

487
00:34:08,813 --> 00:34:11,112
It was dark outside
and the lights were off

488
00:34:11,283 --> 00:34:12,410
in the Camerons' house.

489
00:34:12,584 --> 00:34:14,610
You were at least 40 yards away,

490
00:34:14,786 --> 00:34:17,255
taking narcotics, which,
according to the prescription,

491
00:34:17,422 --> 00:34:18,913
would have affected
your perceptions,

492
00:34:19,090 --> 00:34:22,857
and still you want us to believe
that you saw this shadowy figure

493
00:34:23,028 --> 00:34:25,759
come running out of the
back of the Camerons' house.

494
00:34:25,931 --> 00:34:30,027
Are you sure it wasn't
just a shadow, Mr. Matlock,

495
00:34:30,535 --> 00:34:33,095
that given the darkness
and your drugged state,

496
00:34:33,271 --> 00:34:35,604
you weren't just
imagining things?

497
00:34:35,774 --> 00:34:38,608
I saw somebody!

498
00:34:41,012 --> 00:34:42,503
Sure.

499
00:34:43,882 --> 00:34:46,181
Nothing further, Your Honor.

500
00:34:46,685 --> 00:34:49,587
And I wasn't peeping.

501
00:35:03,401 --> 00:35:04,869
Hi.

502
00:35:08,473 --> 00:35:10,533
Why don't we do it the easy way?

503
00:35:20,952 --> 00:35:22,113
What's in the mail?

504
00:35:22,287 --> 00:35:24,813
I don't know what
you're talking about.

505
00:35:25,924 --> 00:35:27,825
You fight with mailmen
on a daily basis?

506
00:35:30,829 --> 00:35:33,230
Why don't we just take a look?

507
00:35:44,542 --> 00:35:45,771
No! CONRAD: Thank you.

508
00:35:45,944 --> 00:35:49,813
- Give me that.
- No, no, no.

509
00:35:55,587 --> 00:35:58,716
"Dear Helaine, I thought
writing you would be better

510
00:35:58,890 --> 00:36:00,170
than showing up on your doorstep

511
00:36:00,325 --> 00:36:03,227
or possibly doing
something I would regret.

512
00:36:03,395 --> 00:36:06,490
Wayne will never love
